Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:35:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] overview: edge auto-scroll for card drags (user feedback
 2026-10-26)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An overview card drag held at the screen edge now slides the column strip
like a tiled move does outside the overview, so a window can be carried to
the far end of a long scrolling layout.

- Cursor::dataDragEdgeScrollTarget accepts the overview card drag while the
  overview is active; data drags AND compositor tiled moves keep the old
  overview exclusion (DnD-overview semantics pinned by
  drag/data_drag_edge_scroll.sh; the MoveGrab-in-overview drag model stays
  deferred — external review S2-1).
- The card-drag motion path drives updateDataDragEdgeScroll(); the edge
  timer refreshes the drop under the stationary pointer through the new
  Overview::refreshDragTarget() (drag/wheel.sh's stationary-target
  contract), and Overview::endDrag cancels the timer.

Validated: tests/harness/checks/drag/overview_card_drag_edge_scroll.sh
(new regression check: post-detach baseline, >50px slide at the edge, drop
after the revealed column) GREEN; controls drag/move_drag_edge_scroll,
drag/data_drag_edge_scroll, drag/wheel, overview/touchpad,
overview/shift_wheel, overview/horizontal_overflow PASS. Falsified:
reverting the cursor.cpp half turns the new check red (1282 -> 1282) while
the untouched axis behavior stays green. clang-format --dry-run -Werror,
just lint (clang-tidy 234/234) and remark --check clean.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
