 2026-10-27)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"the feature is missing for vertical workspace; horizontal and vertical
scroll could use the same mechanic": during a held overview card drag only
the layout strip had motion — the workspace filmstrip (the rows along the
workspace axis) was inert. It now gets the same two behaviors, pan-only:

- Edge auto-scroll: input.drag_edge_scroll's mechanic (zones, delay, speed
  ramp, timer) drives a second sink — the rows slide at the workspace-axis
  screen edges and the drop re-resolves under the stationary pointer
  (Overview::advanceFilmstripEdgeScroll converts the ramp's screen px/s to
  rows through the preview step so the visible slide matches the strip's).
  Both sinks share the machine's timeline; a corner push scrolls both
  dimensions, and the strip keeps the same behaviour for data drags and
  tiled moves.
- Finger-scroll: updateNavigation's row branch follows the fingers under a
  held card again (it refused all travel), and endNavigation settles the pan
  snap-only — no group->select and no active-workspace switch under the hold
  (the drop's focus activates its destination, like any cross-workspace
  drop). The S2-2 release settle contract is preserved.
- The filmstrip's extreme gaps were dead drop zones (the strip axis got its
  fix with the overhanging-cards contract): workspaceAtPoint's drag
  targeting now extends the end rows' bands to the output edges, so a card
  released past the last preview drops on the end workspace. Insertion gaps
  keep priority.

Validated: drag/overview_card_workspace_axis_pan.sh (one row of pan under
the hold, drop on workspace 2, active workspace unchanged mid-hold, focus
kept) and drag/overview_card_workspace_edge_scroll.sh (both arrangements:
bottom edge with the vertical workspace axis, right edge with the horizontal
one — drop on the far workspace) GREEN; the new
drag/overview_card_drag_edge_scroll_vertical.sh pins the axis-generic
layout-strip twin. Falsified both new halves: refusing the row pan turns the
pan check red, disabling the row edge sink turns the edge check red.
Controls green: the three overview_card strip checks, drag/move_drag_edge_scroll,
drag/data_drag_edge_scroll, drag/wheel, overview/touchpad,
overview/shift_wheel, overview/horizontal_overflow — and the full
drag/+overview/ suite passes except pre-existing reds (drag/floating_release_settle
fails identically at upstream base d9497f36; the two untracked
MoveGrab research loops pin the deferred §3.3 defect). clang-tidy 234/234,
just format clean.

